  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-04-12T02:04:21.011Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hi, i think we all know that .png pictures take quite a bit of space on your disk, specially when you are one of those people who like to take a ton of pictures of moments on vrchat. \nMy suggestion is that, instead of png, use jpg, as pictures will go from 2-3mb to 500-800kb. Yes, we loose a bit of quality, due to compression, but i don't really think its relevant to pictures taken in 1920x1080... There's other games that use jpg format, and we can't see any kind of quality loss, like black desert. \nEven if we had some kind of toggle, between the png and jpg formats would be something. \nThis would help with people with poor internet too, to be able to share moments with their friends.\nAnd yes, we could convert this ourselves, but i think its nice for the game to do this kinda things for us, and make our life easier",
